<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 30.5 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in February 1997 versus 26.5 million lbs in January and 35.4 million lbs in February 1996 the Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1997 period amounted to 57.0 million lbs versus 65.9 million lbs in the 1996 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
